{# =========================================================================
   Typesense Pro - field mapping (the flagship)
   =========================================================================
   The collection's mapping is a real Craft field layout: drag the source's
   fields (and the asset pseudo, Commerce variant, and computed fields from the
   palette) into the layout to index them, and open a field's slideout to tune
   its Typesense mapping (facet, sort, search weight, infix, stemming, locale, a
   bounded type override, and a natural-language description). The control set is
   server-authoritative, derived from each field's Typesense type. The layout
   serialises into the collection definition in project config, exactly like an
   entry type.

   @var definition   CollectionDefinition
   @var designerHtml string  the rendered Craft.FieldLayoutDesigner
   @var readOnly     bool
   @var navItems     array  the collection edit screen's permission-filtered nav
   ========================================================================= #}
{% extends 'typesense/collections/_layout' %}

{% set selectedNavItem = 'mapping' %}
{% set fullPageForm = not readOnly %}

{% block content %}
    {% if readOnly %}
        <div class="readable">
            <blockquote class="note">{{ 'The mapping is read-only because allowAdminChanges is disabled in this environment.'|t('typesense') }}</blockquote>
        </div>
        <hr>
    {% endif %}

    {{ actionInput('typesense/collections/save-mapping') }}
    {{ hiddenInput('uid', definition.uid) }}

    <p class="light">
        {{ 'Place a field in the layout to index it, then open its slideout to tune the Typesense mapping. The type and the available options are derived by the server; the slideout only offers what applies to each field.'|t('typesense') }}
    </p>

    {{ designerHtml|raw }}
{% endblock %}
